  "id": "tactual-localization",
  "term": "tactual localization",
  "definition": "Tactual localization is the ability to identify where on the body a touch is felt. In this historical account, it is explained as depending on a distinct sensory “local sign,” and in some cases as being helped by learned association with vision.",
